    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d213">

                <pb facs="0296" n="230" sameAs="frus:frus1934v05/pg230"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">816.01/363: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Costa Rica</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Sack</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Acting
                        Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">San
                                José</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-01-16T14:00:00-06:00">January 16, 1934—2
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 4:47 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3. In accordance with suggestions contained in your telegram No. 1, January 12, 5
                        p.m.,<anchor n="9" xml:id="d213-f1"/> I had occasion today to informally
                    discuss Central <pb facs="0297" n="231" xml:id="pg231"/> American developments
                    with President Jimenez and Foreign Minister Pacheco. Both expressed delight at
                    President Sacasa’s activities and promised fullest Costa Rican cooperation.
                    Repeated to Managua.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sack</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
